WEBVTT

NOTE request-scan-data: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:06.914
A course that has fallen behind TurfRad
does not have to wait for the next

V0-2
00:00:07.014 --> 00:00:11.460
automatic retrieval. Ask for the latest
scan data, and reload when it is ready.

V1a-1
00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:18.300
Every station row carries the
date its reading was captured.

V1b-1
00:00:18.857 --> 00:00:22.926
One stale row is a station. A column
of stale dates is the whole course,

V1b-2
00:00:23.026 --> 00:00:26.417
and that is a supply problem
rather than a settings problem.

V2a-1
00:00:33.013 --> 00:00:35.253
The circular-arrow button in the toolbar's

V2a-2
00:00:35.353 --> 00:00:37.753
right-hand group is
Request latest scan data.

V2b-1
00:00:38.313 --> 00:00:42.895
It asks Spatial Adjust to fetch the
latest scan data TurfRad already holds.

V2b-2
00:00:42.995 --> 00:00:46.844
It does not order a new scan,
it does not reload the dashboard,

V2b-3
00:00:46.944 --> 00:00:50.123
and it does not change a
single calculation setting.

V3a-1
00:00:57.430 --> 00:00:59.982
The request is queued and you are told so.

V3a-2
00:01:00.082 --> 00:01:04.580
Retrieval may take several minutes,
and you are notified when it is ready.

V3b-1
00:01:05.097 --> 00:01:07.843
You can carry on reading
the table while it runs.

V3b-2
00:01:07.943 --> 00:01:11.307
Nothing is frozen, and nothing
is lost if you navigate away.

V4a-1
00:01:18.373 --> 00:01:21.215
When the retrieval finishes,
a banner says so,

V4a-2
00:01:21.315 --> 00:01:23.787
whether or not TurfRad had a newer scan.

V4a-3
00:01:23.887 --> 00:01:28.523
Reload Data pulls it into the dashboard,
and every suggestion recalculates.

V4b-1
00:01:29.023 --> 00:01:32.892
Dismiss closes the banner and leaves
you on the data you already had.

V4b-2
00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:36.413
The new scan is not thrown away;
it is simply not loaded yet.

V5a-1
00:01:43.693 --> 00:01:48.122
A failed request says so straight away
rather than silently doing nothing.

V5a-2
00:01:48.222 --> 00:01:51.992
If it keeps failing, the diagnostics
dialog reports whether the

V5a-3
00:01:52.092 --> 00:01:56.163
organisation has TurfRad access and
whether it has scan data at all.

V5b-1
00:01:56.727 --> 00:01:59.665
A course-wide problem
is almost always there,

V5b-2
00:01:59.765 --> 00:02:03.357
rather than in your settings.
Check the last scan date.
